(   rho\(nu\) = \(A21 / B21\) / [ \(N1 / N2\) * \(B12 / B21\) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Applying Boltzmann Statistics:) Tj
T*
(   - The population ratio in thermal equilibrium is governed by Boltzmann's law:) Tj
T*
(   N1 / N2 = exp\( \(E2 - E1\) / \(k_B * T\) \) = exp\( h*nu / \(k_B * T\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Substituting into the expression for rho\(nu\):) Tj
T*
(   rho\(nu\) = \(A21 / B21\) / [ \(B12 / B21\) * exp\( h*nu / \(k_B * T\) \) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Comparison with Planck's Blackbody Radiation Law:) Tj
T*
(   - Planck's formula: rho\(nu\) = \(8 * pi * h * nu^3 / c^3\) / [ exp\( h*nu / \(k_B * T\) \) - 1 ].) Tj
T*
(   - For both equations to hold universally across all frequencies nu and temperatures T:) Tj
T*
(   \(i\) B12 / B21 = 1 => B12 = B21 \(Transition probabilities for absorption and stimulated emission) Tj
T*
(   are equal for non-degenerate states\).) Tj
T*
(   \(ii\) A21 / B21 = 8 * pi * h * nu^3 / c^3.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   6. Physical Conclusions:) Tj
T*
(   - Ratio A21/B21 scales as nu^3. At optical and UV frequencies \(large nu\), spontaneous emission) Tj
T*
(   dominates strongly over stimulated emission under thermal conditions, explaining why population) Tj
T*
(   inversion requires active artificial pumping.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
