BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the necessity of population inversion and metastable states for sustained lasing action. Why is lasing impossible in a two-level system under steady-state conditions?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Population Inversion Concept:) Tj
T*
(   - Under normal thermal equilibrium at temperature T, Boltzmann's law dictates:) Tj
T*
(   N2 / N1 = exp\(-Delta_E / \(k_B * T\)\) < 1, hence N1 > N2 always.) Tj
T*
(   - Light passing through such a medium experiences net attenuation: dI = \(N2*B21 - N1*B12\) *) Tj
T*
(   h*nu * I * dz < 0 \(Absorption exceeds emission\).) Tj
T*
(   - To achieve optical amplification \(gain > 0\), we require N2 > N1 \(Population Inversion\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Role of Metastable States:) Tj
T*
(   - Normal atomic excited states decay within tau ~ 10^-8 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Metastable states have forbidden dipole transitions to lower levels, extending their) Tj
T*
(   lifetimes to tau_m ~ 10^-4 to 10^-2 s \(10,000 times longer!\).) Tj
T*
(   - This prolonged lifetime acts as a reservoir, allowing atoms to accumulate in large numbers) Tj
T*
(   faster than they decay, thereby sustaining N2 > N1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Impossibility of Lasing in a Two-Level System:) Tj
T*
(   - In a two-level system with ground state E1 and excited state E2, pumping transitions are) Tj
T*
(   driven by incident radiation of frequency nu = \(E2 - E1\)/h.) Tj
T*
(   - Rate of optical pumping: R_pump = B12 * N1 * rho\(nu\).) Tj
T*
(   - Rate of stimulated depumping: R_depump = B21 * N2 * rho\(nu\).) Tj
T*
(   - Since B12 = B21, as pumping intensity rho\(nu\) -> infinity:) Tj
T*
(   R_pump = R_depump => N1 = N2 \(Optical Saturation / Transparency\).) Tj
T*
(   - The upward and downward transition rates become equal; it is mathematically impossible to) Tj
T*
(   force N2 > N1 in a steady two-level system.) Tj
T*
(   - Therefore, practical lasers must employ at least a 3-level or 4-level energy architecture.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
