(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Three-Level Laser System \(e.g., Ruby Laser\):) Tj
T*
(   - Energy levels: Ground state E1, Pump band E3, Metastable upper laser level E2.) Tj
T*
(   - Operation:) Tj
T*
(   * Atoms pumped from E1 to E3 by optical flashlamp.) Tj
T*
(   * Rapid non-radiative decay from E3 to E2 \(tau_32 ~ 10^-11 s\).) Tj
T*
(   * Lasing transition occurs between E2 and E1 \(ground state\).) Tj
T*
(   - Inherent Drawback:) Tj
T*
(   * The lower laser level E1 is the densely populated ground state containing initially 100% of) Tj
T*
(   all atoms.) Tj
T*
(   * To achieve population inversion N2 > N1, more than 50% of the entire atom population must be) Tj
T*
(   pumped out of the ground state into E2 before any optical gain occurs.) Tj
T*
(   * Requires immense pump power; operates primarily in pulsed mode.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Four-Level Laser System \(e.g., Nd:YAG, He-Ne Laser\):) Tj
T*
(   - Energy levels: Ground state E0, Pump band E3, Upper laser level E2 \(metastable\), Lower laser) Tj
T*
(   level E1.) Tj
T*
(   - Operation:) Tj
T*
(   * Pumping excites atoms from E0 to E3.) Tj
T*
(   * Fast non-radiative decay from E3 into metastable state E2.) Tj
T*
(   * Lasing occurs between E2 and E1.) Tj
T*
(   * Extremely fast non-radiative decay from E1 down to ground state E0 \(tau_10 ~ 10^-11 s\).) Tj
T*
(   - Decisive Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   * Because E1 is separated from ground state E0 by several k_B*T, its thermal population is) Tj
T*
(   virtually zero: N1 ~= 0.) Tj
T*
(   * Any tiny accumulation of atoms in E2 immediately creates N2 > N1.) Tj
T*
(   * Threshold pump power is lower by orders of magnitude.) Tj
T*
(   * Readily operates in continuous-wave \(CW\) mode with high wall-plug efficiency.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
