(   [Problem Statement]: Describe the construction, working principle, and energy level diagram of a Helium-Neon \(He-Ne\) gas laser. Explain the role of helium atoms and tube bore diameter.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Construction Details:) Tj
T*
(   - Active Medium: Gas mixture of Helium and Neon in approximately 10:1 ratio at low total) Tj
T*
(   pressure \(~ 1 torr = 133 Pa\).) Tj
T*
(   - Discharge Tube: Narrow capillary tube of hard borosilicate glass or fused silica with bore) Tj
T*
(   diameter ~ 1 to 2 mm and length ~ 20 to 50 cm.) Tj
T*
(   - Optical Cavity: Enclosed by two mirrors \(one 100% reflective, one 98-99% output coupler\).) Tj
T*
(   Tube ends terminate in Brewster angle windows \(theta_B ~= 56 deg\) to eliminate reflection loss) Tj
T*
(   and linearly polarize the beam.) Tj
T*
(   - Electrical Excitation: DC high voltage \(~ 1.5 to 2.5 kV\) applied across anode and cold) Tj
T*
(   aluminum cathode to ignite glow discharge.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Working Mechanism and Energy Level Kinetics:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Electron Impact Excitation of He:) Tj
T*
(   Energetic discharge electrons collide with ground-state He atoms, raising them to long-lived) Tj
T*
(   metastable levels 2^1S \(20.61 eV\) and 2^3S \(19.81 eV\):) Tj
T*
(   e- + He -> He* \(2^1S, 2^3S\) + e-.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Resonant Collision Energy Transfer to Ne:) Tj
T*
(   The 2^1S and 2^3S levels of He coincide almost perfectly in energy with the 3s and 2s levels of) Tj
T*
(   Ne \(3s2 at 20.66 eV and 2s2 at 19.78 eV\).) Tj
T*
(   During inelastic collisions of the second kind, energy is transferred with high cross-section) Tj
T*
