T*
(   3. Lasing Threshold Condition:) Tj
T*
(   - For self-sustained optical oscillation, the round-trip gain must exactly compensate for all) Tj
T*
(   round-trip losses:) Tj
T*
(   I_round_trip >= I_0 => R1 * R2 * exp\( 2 * \(gamma_th - alpha\) * L \) = 1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Solving for Threshold Gain gamma_th:) Tj
T*
(   - Take natural logarithm of both sides:) Tj
T*
(   ln\(R1 * R2\) + 2 * \(gamma_th - alpha\) * L = 0.) Tj
T*
(   - Rearranging:) Tj
T*
(   2 * \(gamma_th - alpha\) * L = - ln\(R1 * R2\) = ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - gamma_th - alpha = \(1 / \(2 * L\)\) * ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \).) Tj
T*
(   - Defining the effective mirror loss coefficient alpha_m = \(1 / \(2 * L\)\) * ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \):) Tj
T*
(   gamma_th = alpha + alpha_m = alpha + \(1 / \(2 * L\)\) * ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Physical Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - Lasing can only ignite when the pump power is high enough that medium gain gamma equals or) Tj
T*
(   exceeds the sum of internal medium losses alpha plus cavity coupling mirror losses alpha_m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
