/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 9:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the optical properties of laser radiation: monochromaticity, coherence \(temporal and spatial\), directionality, and brightness. Give mathematical definitions for each.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Monochromaticity:) Tj
T*
(   - Conventional light sources emit across a broad band \(Delta_lambda ~ 10-100 nm\). Laser light) Tj
T*
(   exhibits an extremely narrow spectral linewidth Delta_nu.) Tj
T*
(   - Monochromaticity is quantified by spectral purity: Q_mono = nu_0 / Delta_nu.) Tj
T*
(   - Stabilized single-mode lasers achieve Delta_nu < 1 kHz, yielding spectral purities exceeding) Tj
T*
(   10^11.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Coherence:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Temporal Coherence: Measures the phase correlation of an optical wave train with itself) Tj
T*
(   at a later time tau:) Tj
T*
(   Coherence time: tau_c = 1 / Delta_nu.) Tj
T*
(   Coherence length: L_c = c * tau_c = c / Delta_nu = lambda^2 / Delta_lambda.) Tj
T*
(   For sunlight L_c ~ 1 micrometer; for He-Ne lasers L_c can exceed several kilometers.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Spatial Coherence: Measures the fixed phase correlation across different lateral spatial) Tj
T*
(   points on the beam wavefront at the same instant.) Tj
T*
(   Determined by mutual coherence function Gamma_12\(tau=0\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Directionality:) Tj
T*
(   - Laser beams emerge with minimal spatial divergence determined purely by diffraction at the) Tj
T*
(   exit aperture:) Tj
T*
(   Divergence angle \(half-angle\): theta_div ~= 1.22 * lambda / D, where D is aperture diameter.) Tj
T*
(   - For lambda = 632.8 nm and D = 2 mm: theta_div ~= 0.38 mrad \(~ 0.02 degrees\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Brightness \(Radiance B\):) Tj
T*
(   - Power emitted per unit surface area per unit solid angle:) Tj
T*
(   B = P / \(A * Omega\) \(W / \(m^2 * sr\)\).) Tj
T*
(   - Because laser power P is concentrated into an exceptionally tiny solid angle Omega = pi *) Tj
T*
(   theta_div^2, a modest 1 mW laser pointer has a brightness orders of magnitude greater than the) Tj
T*
(   surface of the Sun.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

endstream
