12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the physical principles and architecture of LiDAR \(Light Detection and Ranging\). How does it generate 3D point clouds for civil terrain and bridge surveying?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Fundamental Principle of LiDAR:) Tj
T*
(   - LiDAR is an active optical remote sensing technology analogous to radar, utilizing short) Tj
T*
(   pulses of laser light \(typically nanosecond pulses at lambda = 905 nm, 1064 nm, or 1550 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - The instrument emits a collimated laser pulse toward a target surface and measures the) Tj
T*
(   round-trip Time-of-Flight \(ToF\) Delta_t taken for backscattered photons to return to an) Tj
T*
(   avalanche photodiode \(APD\) detector.) Tj
T*
(   - Range distance d: d = c * Delta_t / \(2 * n_air\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. System Architecture Components:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Pulsed Laser Transmitter: High repetition rate \(100 kHz - 2 MHz\) laser engine.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Optical Scanning Mechanism: Rotating polygon mirror, oscillating galvo mirror, or MEMS) Tj
T*
(   mirror to sweep the laser beam across the swath.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) High-Speed Timing Unit: Picosecond time-to-digital converters \(TDC\) achieving millimeter) Tj
T*
(   ranging accuracy.) Tj
T*
(   - \(d\) Integrated GNSS and IMU: For mobile/airborne platforms, differential GPS tracks sensor) Tj
T*
(   position \(X, Y, Z\) and Inertial Measurement Unit \(IMU\) logs pitch, roll, and heading \(omega,) Tj
T*
(   phi, kappa\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Generation of 3D Point Clouds:) Tj
T*
(   - By combining measured range d, beam scan angle theta, and real-time sensor coordinates from) Tj
T*
(   GNSS/IMU, the direct georeferencing equation computes exact 3D Cartesian coordinates \(X, Y, Z\)) Tj
T*
(   for each reflection.) Tj
T*
(   - Millions of individual points per minute form a dense 3D point cloud.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Surveying Applications:) Tj
T*
(   - Digital Elevation Models \(DEM\) and contour maps of steep mountainous highway alignments.) Tj
T*
(   - As-built BIM documentation of complex historic bridges and tunnels.) Tj
T*
(   - Structural deformation monitoring of dam embankments and open-pit mining slopes.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 11:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the optical mechanism and precision of Electronic Distance Measurement \(EDM\) used in modern surveying Total Stations.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. EDM Working Principle:) Tj
T*
(   - Total Station EDM instruments measure distances up to several kilometers with millimeter) Tj
T*
(   accuracy using modulated infrared or visible laser carriers.) Tj
T*
(   - Two primary measurement principles exist:) Tj
T*
(   * Pulse Time-of-Flight \(for reflectorless long-range measurement\).) Tj
T*
(   * Phase-Shift Comparison \(for highest geodetic precision\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mathematical Formulation of Phase-Shift EDM:) Tj
T*
(   - A continuous laser diode beam is amplitude-modulated at a precise radio frequency f_m \(e.g.,) Tj
T*
(   15 MHz or 150 MHz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Modulation wavelength: lambda_m = c / f_m.) Tj
T*
(   - The modulated beam travels distance d to a retroreflector prism and returns, traversing total) Tj
T*
(   path 2*d.) Tj
T*
(   - Total path length in terms of modulation wavelength:) Tj
T*
(   2 * d = N * lambda_m + Delta_lambda,) Tj
T*
