(   [Problem Statement]: A 632.8 nm He-Ne laser has a cavity length of 30 cm and mirror reflectivities R1 = 1.0 and R2 = 0.98. If the single-pass internal scattering loss is 1%, calculate: \(a\) longitudinal mode separation, \(b\) photon lifetime in the cavity, \(c\) threshold gain coefficient gamma_th.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Wavelength lambda = 632.8 nm = 6.328 x 10^-7 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Cavity length L = 0.30 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Mirror reflectivities: R1 = 1.0, R2 = 0.98.) Tj
T*
(   - Fractional internal loss per pass: delta_loss = 0.01 => alpha * L = 0.01 => alpha = 0.01 /) Tj
T*
(   0.30 = 0.0333 m^-1.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light: c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Longitudinal Mode Separation Delta_nu:) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_nu = c / \(2 * L\) = \(3.0 x 10^8 m/s\) / \(2 * 0.30 m\) = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / 0.60 = 5.0 x 10^8) Tj
T*
(   Hz = 500 MHz.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Photon Lifetime tau_p:) Tj
T*
(   - Round-trip cavity transit time: t_RT = 2 * L / c = 0.60 / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 2.0 x 10^-9 s = 2.0) Tj
T*
(   ns.) Tj
T*
(   - Total fractional round-trip loss: delta_RT = 2 * alpha * L + ln\(1 / \(R1 * R2\)\).) Tj
T*
(   ln\(1 / \(1.0 * 0.98\)\) = ln\(1.0204\) = 0.0202.) Tj
T*
(   delta_RT = 2 * \(0.01\) + 0.0202 = 0.0402.) Tj
T*
(   - Photon cavity lifetime:) Tj
T*
(   tau_p = t_RT / delta_RT = \(2.0 x 10^-9 s\) / 0.0402 = 4.975 x 10^-8 s = 49.75 ns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Threshold Gain Coefficient gamma_th:) Tj
T*
(   - gamma_th = alpha + \(1 / \(2 * L\)\) * ln\( 1 / \(R1 * R2\) \)) Tj
T*
(   - gamma_th = 0.0333 + \(1 / 0.60\) * 0.0202 = 0.0333 + 0.0337 = 0.0670 m^-1.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
