(   [Problem Statement]: A pulsed Nd:YAG laser \(lambda = 1064 nm\) generates pulses of energy 250 mJ with duration 8.0 ns at repetition rate 10 Hz. Calculate: \(a\) peak pulse power, \(b\) average power, \(c\) number of photons per pulse, \(d\) peak electric field if focused to a 100 micrometer diameter spot.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Pulse energy E_p = 250 mJ = 0.250 J; Duration Delta_t = 8.0 ns = 8.0 x 10^-9 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Repetition rate f_rep = 10 Hz; Wavelength lambda = 1064 nm = 1.064 x 10^-6 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Focused spot diameter d = 100 micrometers = 1.0 x 10^-4 m; radius r = 5.0 x 10^-5 m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Peak Pulse Power P_peak:) Tj
T*
(   - P_peak = E_p / Delta_t = 0.250 J / \(8.0 x 10^-9 s\) = 3.125 x 10^7 Watts = 31.25 MW.) Tj
T*
