/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain Q-switching in lasers. Describe the working mechanism of active \(electro-optic Pockels cell\) and passive \(saturable absorber\) Q-switches.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Concept of Q-Switching \(Quality-Factor Switching\):) Tj
T*
(   - The Quality factor Q of an optical cavity represents the ratio of stored energy to energy) Tj
T*
(   dissipated per cycle:) Tj
T*
(   Q = 2 * pi * \(Stored Energy\) / \(Energy Dissipated per Cycle\).) Tj
T*
(   - Q-switching is an optical technique to generate giant nanosecond pulses with multi-megawatt) Tj
T*
(   peak powers.) Tj
T*
(   - Technique sequence:) Tj
T*
(   * Step 1: Cavity Q is held at an artificially low value \(high losses\) while the active medium) Tj
T*
(   is heavily pumped.) Tj
T*
(   * Since lasing is suppressed, population inversion N2 - N1 accumulates to an enormous level far) Tj
T*
(   above normal threshold.) Tj
T*
(   * Step 2: The cavity Q is abruptly switched to a high value \(losses removed\) in a few) Tj
T*
(   nanoseconds.) Tj
T*
(   * The massive stored inversion discharges instantaneously in a single, colossal optical pulse.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Active Q-Switching via Electro-Optic Pockels Cell:) Tj
T*
(   - A Pockels cell crystal \(e.g., KD*P, Lithium Niobate\) and a linear polarizer are placed inside) Tj
T*
(   the cavity.) Tj
T*
(   - When high quarter-wave voltage V_pi/4 is applied, the crystal induces a 90-degree round-trip) Tj
T*
(   phase retardation, rotating polarization by 90 degrees.) Tj
T*
(   - The cross-polarized light is rejected by the polarizer \(low Q state\).) Tj
T*
(   - When maximum inversion is reached, the voltage is shorted to zero in < 5 ns, instantly) Tj
T*
(   restoring full transmission \(high Q state\) and releasing the giant pulse.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Passive Q-Switching via Saturable Absorber:) Tj
T*
(   - Utilizes a non-linear dye or doped crystal \(e.g., Cr4+:YAG\) that absorbs light strongly at) Tj
T*
(   low intensities.) Tj
T*
(   - As spontaneous fluorescence builds up, upper levels of the absorber saturate \('bleach'\),) Tj
T*
(   becoming completely transparent at threshold.) Tj
T*
(   - Self-triggers automatic Q-switched pulses without external electronic timing.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
