/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the working principles of Laser Doppler Vibrometry \(LDV\) and describe how it is used for non-contact dynamic health monitoring of bridges and structures.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Working Principle of LDV:) Tj
T*
(   - Laser Doppler Vibrometry \(LDV\) is an optical interferometric technique that measures the) Tj
T*
(   instantaneous velocity and displacement of a vibrating structural surface without physical mass) Tj
T*
(   loading.) Tj
T*
(   - An internal helium-neon or diode laser beam is split into a reference beam and an) Tj
T*
(   interrogation target beam.) Tj
T*
(   - The target beam is directed onto a vibrating structural element \(e.g., bridge stay-cable,) Tj
T*
(   concrete girder, steel truss\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Doppler Shift Physics:) Tj
T*
(   - If the structural surface moves along the beam axis with instantaneous velocity v\(t\), the) Tj
T*
(   reflected light experiences a Doppler frequency shift:) Tj
T*
(   f_D\(t\) = 2 * v\(t\) / lambda.) Tj
T*
(   - For He-Ne laser \(lambda = 632.8 nm\): A velocity of v = 1 mm/s yields f_D = 3.16 kHz.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Heterodyne Optical Detection:) Tj
T*
(   - To resolve both direction and magnitude of motion, an acousto-optic modulator \(Bragg cell\)) Tj
T*
(   shifts the reference beam frequency by f_B \(typically 40 MHz\).) Tj
T*
(   - Recombining reference and reflected beams at the photodetector generates a carrier beat) Tj
T*
(   signal at f = f_B +- f_D\(t\).) Tj
T*
(   - Demodulation delivers the real-time velocity waveform v\(t\) and displacement x\(t\) = Integral) Tj
T*
(   v\(t\) dt with sub-micrometer resolution.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Civil Structural Health Monitoring Utility:) Tj
T*
(   - Cable-Stayed Bridge Tension Estimation: Determines cable natural resonant frequencies) Tj
T*
(   non-contact from distances > 100 m, from which cable tensile force is computed via string) Tj
T*
(   vibration theory.) Tj
T*
(   - Seismic Response Analysis: Maps full-field mode shapes and damping ratios of bridge piers) Tj
T*
(   under ambient traffic and seismic excitations.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F2 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(>> Solution to Question 16:) Tj
T*
ET
BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A laser beam of wavelength lambda = 632.8 nm has an initial waist radius w_0 = 1.5 mm. Calculate: \(a\) Rayleigh range z_R, \(b\) beam divergence half-angle theta_div, \(c\) beam spot radius at distance z = 100 m, \(d\) beam spot radius at distance z = 1.0 km.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Formulas for Gaussian Beam Propagation:) Tj
T*
(   - Rayleigh range: z_R = pi * w_0^2 / lambda) Tj
T*
(   - Far-field divergence half-angle: theta_div = lambda / \(pi * w_0\)) Tj
T*
(   - Spot radius at distance z: w\(z\) = w_0 * sqrt\( 1 + \(z / z_R\)^2 \)) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Rayleigh Range z_R:) Tj
T*
(   - w_0 = 1.5 x 10^-3 m; lambda = 6.328 x 10^-7 m.) Tj
T*
(   - z_R = pi * \(1.5 x 10^-3\)^2 / \(6.328 x 10^-7\) = pi * \(2.25 x 10^-6\) / \(6.328 x 10^-7\) = 7.0686) Tj
T*
(   x 10^-6 / 6.328 x 10^-7 = 11.17 meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Beam Divergence Half-Angle theta_div:) Tj
T*
(   - theta_div = lambda / \(pi * w_0\) = \(6.328 x 10^-7\) / \(pi * 1.5 x 10^-3\) = 1.343 x 10^-4) Tj
T*
(   radians = 0.1343 mrad.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
ET

