() Tj
T*
(   2. Electronic Speckle Pattern Interferometry \(ESPI\):) Tj
T*
(   - ESPI combines laser speckle photography with holographic interferometry.) Tj
T*
(   - A coherent laser beam is split into an object beam illuminating the concrete specimen and a) Tj
T*
(   reference beam directed to a CCD/CMOS sensor.) Tj
T*
(   - The interference of the speckle field with the smooth reference beam forms an initial speckle) Tj
T*
(   interferogram \(reference state\).) Tj
T*
(   - When the structural concrete is subjected to thermal, mechanical, or acoustic loading,) Tj
T*
(   surface points undergo sub-micrometer displacements.) Tj
T*
(   - A second speckle pattern is recorded. Digital subtraction of the two speckle images yields) Tj
T*
(   correlation fringe patterns.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Detection of Micro-Cracks and Debonding:) Tj
T*
(   - In a sound concrete section, fringe lines are continuous, smooth, and evenly spaced.) Tj
T*
(   - Around internal micro-cracks, localized delaminations, or rebar slip zones, stress) Tj
T*
(   concentrations cause discontinuous jumps and disruptions in the fringe field.) Tj
T*
(   - Enables full-field, non-destructive visualization of sub-surface micro-crack initiation long) Tj
T*
(   before visible macro-cracking occurs.) Tj
