12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: A LiDAR system flies at an altitude of H = 1500 m with ground speed 60 m/s. The scanner emits 200,000 pulses per second over a scan swath of +- 20 degrees. Calculate: \(a\) swath width on the ground, \(b\) average footprint spacing, \(c\) maximum round-trip travel time.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Parameters:) Tj
T*
(   - Altitude H = 1500 m; Ground speed v = 60 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Pulse repetition frequency PRF = 200 kHz = 200,000 pulses/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Half scan angle theta_half = 20 degrees \(Total field of view FOV = 40 degrees\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Swath Width W on Ground:) Tj
T*
(   - W = 2 * H * tan\(theta_half\) = 2 * 1500 * tan\(20 deg\).) Tj
T*
(   - tan\(20 deg\) = 0.36397.) Tj
T*
(   - W = 2 * 1500 * 0.36397 = 1091.9 meters \(~ 1.09 km\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Average Footprint Point Density and Spacing:) Tj
T*
(   - Area covered per second: A_rate = W * v = 1091.9 m * 60 m/s = 65,514 m^2/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Number of pulses per second = 200,000.) Tj
T*
(   - Point density rho_pts = 200,000 / 65,514 = 3.05 points/m^2.) Tj
T*
(   - Average point spacing: s = 1 / sqrt\(rho_pts\) = 1 / sqrt\(3.05\) = 0.573 m = 57.3 cm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Maximum Round-Trip Travel Time t_max:) Tj
T*
(   - Longest range occurs at maximum scan angle \(edge of swath\):) Tj
T*
(   R_max = H / cos\(theta_half\) = 1500 / cos\(20 deg\) = 1500 / 0.93969 = 1596.3 meters.) Tj
T*
(   - Two-way travel time:) Tj
T*
(   t_max = 2 * R_max / c = 2 * 1596.3 / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 3192.6 / \(3.0 x 10^8\) = 1.064 x 10^-5 s =) Tj
T*
(   10.64 microseconds.) Tj
T*
(   - Since pulse interval is T_pulse = 1 / PRF = 5.0 microseconds, multi-pulse-in-the-air \(MPiA\)) Tj
T*
(   processing is required.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
