12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Calculate the coherence length and coherence time for: \(a\) a sodium vapor lamp emitting at 589 nm with spectral width 0.01 nm, \(b\) a He-Ne laser emitting at 632.8 nm with linewidth 1.0 MHz, \(c\) an ultra-stable fiber laser with linewidth 1.0 kHz.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Formulas:) Tj
T*
(   - Frequency linewidth from wavelength linewidth: Delta_nu = c * Delta_lambda / lambda^2) Tj
T*
(   - Coherence time: tau_c = 1 / Delta_nu) Tj
T*
(   - Coherence length: L_c = c * tau_c = c / Delta_nu = lambda^2 / Delta_lambda) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Sodium Vapor Lamp \(lambda = 589 nm = 5.89 x 10^-7 m, Delta_lambda = 0.01 nm = 10^-11 m\):) Tj
T*
(   - Delta_nu = \(3.0 x 10^8 * 10^-11\) / \(5.89 x 10^-7\)^2 = 3.0 x 10^-3 / 3.469 x 10^-13 = 8.647 x) Tj
T*
(   10^9 Hz ~= 8.65 GHz.) Tj
T*
(   - tau_c = 1 / \(8.647 x 10^9\) = 1.156 x 10^-10 s = 0.116 ns.) Tj
T*
(   - L_c = \(5.89 x 10^-7\)^2 / 10^-11 = 3.469 x 10^-13 / 10^-11 = 0.0347 m = 3.47 cm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) He-Ne Laser \(Delta_nu = 1.0 MHz = 10^6 Hz, lambda = 632.8 nm\):) Tj
T*
(   - tau_c = 1 / 10^6 = 1.0 x 10^-6 s = 1.0 microsecond.) Tj
T*
(   - L_c = c / Delta_nu = \(3.0 x 10^8 m/s\) / 10^6 s^-1 = 300 meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Ultra-Stable Fiber Laser \(Delta_nu = 1.0 kHz = 10^3 Hz\):) Tj
T*
(   - tau_c = 1 / 10^3 = 1.0 x 10^-3 s = 1.0 millisecond.) Tj
T*
(   - L_c = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / 10^3 = 3.0 x 10^5 meters = 300 kilometers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Engineering Significance:) Tj
T*
(   - Sodium lamp coherence \(3.5 cm\) fails for surveying interference. The 300 km coherence length) Tj
T*
(   of single-frequency fiber lasers enables kilometer-scale structural interferometers on bridges) Tj
T*
ET

endstream
