12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Discuss laser safety classifications \(Class 1 to Class 4\) per IEC 60825-1 and OSHA standards, and outline mandatory safety protocols for civil construction sites.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Laser Safety Classification \(IEC 60825-1 / ANSI Z136\):) Tj
T*
(   - Class 1: Safe under all reasonably foreseeable conditions \(e.g., enclosed CD-ROM, fully) Tj
T*
(   contained survey instrument\).) Tj
T*
(   - Class 2: Visible lasers \(400-700 nm\) with output power <= 1 mW. Eye protection afforded by) Tj
T*
(   normal human blink reflex \(aversion response time ~ 0.25 s\). Includes standard laser pointers) Tj
T*
(   and indoor levels.) Tj
T*
(   - Class 3R: Output power 1 mW to 5 mW. Low risk of ocular injury if exposure is brief, but) Tj
T*
(   direct intrabeam viewing is hazardous.) Tj
T*
(   - Class 3B: Output power 5 mW to 500 mW. Direct beam and specular reflections cause immediate,) Tj
T*
(   permanent retinal damage. Diffuse reflections generally safe.) Tj
T*
(   - Class 4: High-power lasers \(> 500 mW\). Can burn human skin, cause devastating eye injury from) Tj
T*
(   both direct and diffuse scattered light, and ignite construction site fires. \(e.g., laser) Tj
T*
(   cutting, demolition ablation\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Mandatory Construction Protocols:) Tj
T*
ET

