(   4. Fractional Distance Measurement Error:) Tj
T*
(   - Measured distance is based on assumed speed: d_meas = c * t / \(2 * n_assumed\).) Tj
T*
(   - Fractional change: Delta_d / d = - Delta_n / n ~= - \(n2 - n1\) = - \(1.0002549 - 1.0002726\) = +) Tj
T*
(   17.7 x 10^-6 = + 17.7 ppm.) Tj
T*
(   - For a 1000 m measured baseline, the uncorrected temperature rise introduces an error of:) Tj
T*
(   Error = 1000 m * 17.7 x 10^-6 = + 0.0177 m = + 17.7 mm.) Tj
T*
(   - This ~1.8 cm error violates millimeter geodetic tolerances, proving that real-time digital) Tj
T*
(   barometric and temperature sensors must feed automatic meteorological compensation into Total) Tj
