BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the optical setup and physical principles of Second Harmonic Generation \(SHG\) used to convert infrared Nd:YAG laser light into visible green laser beams for surveying.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Non-Linear Optical Physics:) Tj
T*
(   - At low electric field strengths, dielectric polarization is linear: P = epsilon_0 * chi^\(1\) *) Tj
T*
(   E.) Tj
T*
(   - Under intense laser electric fields \(~ 10^7 - 10^9 V/m\), higher-order non-linear polarization) Tj
T*
(   terms become prominent:) Tj
T*
(   P = epsilon_0 * [ chi^\(1\) * E + chi^\(2\) * E^2 + chi^\(3\) * E^3 + ... ],) Tj
T*
(   where chi^\(2\) is the second-order non-linear optical susceptibility.) Tj
T*
(   - Second-order non-linearity requires crystals lacking inversion symmetry \(non-centrosymmetric) Tj
T*
(   crystals, such as KTP, LiNbO3, BBO\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Generation of 2*omega Frequency Component:) Tj
T*
(   - Let the input fundamental wave from an Nd:YAG laser be E\(t\) = E_0 * cos\(omega*t\) \(lambda =) Tj
T*
(   1064 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - The quadratic polarization term is:) Tj
T*
(   P^\(2\)\(t\) = epsilon_0 * chi^\(2\) * [ E_0 * cos\(omega*t\) ]^2 = 0.5 * epsilon_0 * chi^\(2\) * E_0^2 *) Tj
T*
(   [ 1 + cos\(2*omega*t\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The time-varying term oscillates at double frequency 2*omega, which re-radiates) Tj
T*
(   electromagnetic radiation at half the fundamental wavelength:) Tj
T*
(   lambda_2 = lambda_1 / 2 = 1064 nm / 2 = 532 nm \(brilliant green light\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Phase-Matching Requirement:) Tj
T*
(   - Efficient energy conversion requires constructive interference between the generated second) Tj
T*
(   harmonic wave and the driving non-linear polarization over crystal length L.) Tj
T*
(   - Phase matching condition: Delta_k = k\(2*omega\) - 2*k\(omega\) = 0 => n\(2*omega\) = n\(omega\).) Tj
T*
(   - Achieved using crystal birefringence \(Type I or Type II phase matching\) by tuning the crystal) Tj
T*
(   orientation angle theta_pm.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Application in Civil Engineering:) Tj
T*
(   - 532 nm green beams match the peak human eye photopic sensitivity \(~ 555 nm\), appearing 4) Tj
T*
(   times brighter than red 635 nm beams of equal power, making green lasers standard for outdoor) Tj
T*
(   surveying and construction site leveling.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
