(   [Problem Statement]: A bathymetric LiDAR survey is conducted over a reservoir with water surface elevation 245.0 m. If the flight altitude is 600 m above water, and laser pulses detect reflections at round-trip times t1 = 4.00 microseconds and t2 = 4.09 microseconds, determine: \(a\) water surface range, \(b\) reservoir bottom depth, \(c\) reservoir bed elevation \(n_water = 1.333\).) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light in air: c_air ~= c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Round-trip time to water surface: t1 = 4.00 microseconds = 4.00 x 10^-6 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Round-trip time to reservoir bottom: t2 = 4.09 microseconds = 4.09 x 10^-6 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Water refractive index: n_w = 1.333.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light in water: v_w = c / n_w = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / 1.333 = 2.25 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
(   - Water surface elevation: H_water = 245.0 m.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. \(a\) Distance from Aircraft to Water Surface d_air:) Tj
T*
(   - d_air = c * t1 / 2 = \(3.0 x 10^8 m/s * 4.00 x 10^-6 s\) / 2 = 1200 / 2 = 600.0 meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. \(b\) Water Depth h_w in Reservoir:) Tj
T*
(   - The additional time delay represents travel through water and back:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_t = t2 - t1 = 4.09 - 4.00 = 0.09 microseconds = 9.0 x 10^-8 s.) Tj
T*
(   - Water depth: h_w = v_w * Delta_t / 2 = \(2.25 x 10^8 m/s * 9.0 x 10^-8 s\) / 2 = 20.25 / 2 =) Tj
T*
(   10.125 meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. \(c\) Reservoir Bed Elevation H_bed:) Tj
T*
(   - H_bed = H_water - h_w = 245.0 m - 10.125 m = 234.875 meters.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   5. Bathymetric LiDAR Mechanism:) Tj
T*
(   - Dual-wavelength LiDAR transmits infrared \(1064 nm\) which reflects sharply from water surface,) Tj
T*
(   and green \(532 nm\) which penetrates the water column to map the underwater bed topography and) Tj
T*
(   sediment siltation.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
