12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Explain the optical construction and operation of a Fiber Laser. Discuss why high-power fiber lasers are increasingly utilized in structural steel fabrication and demolition.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Optical Architecture of Fiber Lasers:) Tj
T*
(   - Active Medium: High-purity silica optical fiber core doped with rare-earth ions \(Ytterbium,) Tj
T*
(   Yb3+ emitting at 1070 nm, or Erbium, Er3+ at 1550 nm\).) Tj
T*
(   - Double-Clad Fiber Geometry:) Tj
T*
(   * Small single-mode core \(diameter ~ 10-25 microns\) containing Yb3+ dopant.) Tj
T*
(   * Surrounding inner cladding \(diameter ~ 250-400 microns\) with non-circular cross-section) Tj
T*
(   \(D-shaped or octagonal\) to guide multimode pump light.) Tj
T*
(   * Low-index outer polymer cladding to confine pump light.) Tj
T*
(   - In-Fiber Resonator: Fiber Bragg Gratings \(FBG\) written directly into the fiber core serve as) Tj
T*
(   100% and output coupler cavity mirrors, eliminating free-space optical alignment.) Tj
T*
(   - Pumping: High-reliability multimode laser diode arrays spliced directly via fused fiber) Tj
T*
(   combiners.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Operating Advantages:) Tj
T*
(   - \(a\) Unsurpassed Beam Quality \(M^2 ~= 1.1\): Delivers diffraction-limited focus over long) Tj
T*
(   working distances.) Tj
T*
(   - \(b\) Superior Thermal Management: The long fiber length \(10 to 50 m\) provides an enormous) Tj
T*
(   surface-area-to-volume ratio, allowing passive air or simple water cooling without thermal) Tj
T*
(   lensing distortion.) Tj
T*
(   - \(c\) High Wall-Plug Efficiency: Achieves 35-45% electrical-to-optical efficiency \(compared to) Tj
T*
(   < 3% for lamp-pumped Nd:YAG or 10% for CO2 lasers\).) Tj
T*
(   - \(d\) Monolithic Rugged Design: No mirrors to misalign; immune to construction vibration,) Tj
T*
ET

