(   [Problem Statement]: A laser distance meter has a measurement baseline of 500 m. If the phase comparator can resolve phase difference to within 0.18 degrees, what modulation frequency f_m is required to achieve a ranging resolution of 0.5 mm?) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Governing Phase-Shift Formula:) Tj
T*
(   - Distance equation: d = \(lambda_m / 4*pi\) * Delta_phi.) Tj
T*
(   - Relating range resolution Delta_d to phase resolution Delta_phi:) Tj
T*
(   Delta_d = \(lambda_m / 4*pi\) * Delta_phi = \(c / \(4 * pi * f_m\)\) * Delta_phi.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Given Data:) Tj
T*
(   - Ranging resolution required: Delta_d = 0.5 mm = 5.0 x 10^-4 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Phase resolution: Delta_phi = 0.18 degrees = 0.18 * \(pi / 180\) = pi / 1000 = 3.1416 x 10^-3) Tj
T*
(   radians.) Tj
T*
(   - Speed of light: c = 3.0 x 10^8 m/s.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   3. Solving for Modulation Frequency f_m:) Tj
T*
(   - f_m = \(c * Delta_phi\) / \(4 * pi * Delta_d\).) Tj
T*
(   - f_m = [ 3.0 x 10^8 * \(pi / 1000\) ] / [ 4 * pi * \(5.0 x 10^-4\) ].) Tj
T*
(   - The factor of pi cancels out:) Tj
T*
(   f_m = [ 3.0 x 10^8 / 1000 ] / [ 2.0 x 10^-3 ] = \(3.0 x 10^5\) / \(2.0 x 10^-3\) = 1.5 x 10^8 Hz =) Tj
T*
(   150 MHz.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   4. Modulation Wavelength lambda_m:) Tj
T*
(   - lambda_m = c / f_m = \(3.0 x 10^8\) / \(1.5 x 10^8\) = 2.0 meters.) Tj
T*
(   - One full cycle of phase \(360 deg\) corresponds to a distance change of lambda_m / 2 = 1.0 m.) Tj
T*
(   - Resolving 1.0 m to 1 part in 2000 \(0.18 deg / 360 deg\) delivers exactly 0.5 mm ranging) Tj
T*
(   precision.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
