BT
/F1 8.5 Tf
12.5 TL
(   [Problem Statement]: Synthesize the technological impact of lasers on the civil engineering industry, contrasting traditional surveying/inspection methods with modern laser-based technologies.) Tj
T*
(   [Detailed Step-by-Step Answer]:) Tj
T*
(   1. Revolution in Civil Surveying and Geodesy:) Tj
T*
(   - Traditional Methods: Plumb bobs subject to wind sway, optical theodolites requiring two-man) Tj
T*
(   chaining crews, leveling rods with human parallax error, and slow point-by-point stadia) Tj
T*
(   measurements.) Tj
T*
(   - Laser Technologies: Robotic Total Stations and electronic distance meters \(EDM\) deliver) Tj
T*
(   millimeter coordinates automatically. Rotating lasers project continuous 360-degree flat datums) Tj
T*
(   across entire construction sites, operating unmanned with grade sensors on earthmoving) Tj
T*
(   bulldozers.) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
(   2. Terrain and As-Built Modeling \(LiDAR\):) Tj
T*
(   - Traditional Methods: Manual ground surveying across hazardous mountainous highway corridors) Tj
T*
